+### Check the platform API used by the rebuild
+
+Record the compiler executable, language level, emitted class-file version, selected platform
+API and test runtime separately. On JDK 25, `javac -source 17 -target 17` without matching
+platform classes can compile `List.of("a").getFirst()` to major 61 using the newer API.
+`--release 17` rejects that call: `List.getFirst()` was introduced in 21. Passing the resulting
+class on JDK 25 does not verify Java 17 compatibility.
+
+Use the actual consumer minimum to choose the API boundary. If 17 is still promised, enforce
+that boundary and replace unsupported calls while preserving behavior, including exceptions.
+If the minimum is already 21, this call needs no rewrite merely because an inherited target
+setting says 17. Use `--release` for the agreed minimum when suitable; builds that need separate
+source/target settings must also select the appropriate platform classes (`--system` for JDK
+9+, per the compiler documentation). Do not raise the consumer baseline to make a build pass.
+Compile-time API checks and runs on the newer VM still leave behavior on an untested older VM
+unverified; report that missing runtime coverage explicitly.
+
